1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,394
They call it a demo.

2
00:00:02,424 --> 00:00:03,983
It is a business.

3
00:00:04,013 --> 00:00:09,412
This API has a price, a treasury, and customers who pay per request.

4
00:00:09,442 --> 00:00:13,874
The key that signs every delivery is not in anyone's pocket.

5
00:00:13,904 --> 00:00:15,855
Nobody is at the keyboard.

6
00:00:16,335 --> 00:00:19,174
Here is the problem with buying software.

7
00:00:19,204 --> 00:00:20,685
You can copy the code.

8
00:00:20,715 --> 00:00:23,214
You cannot copy the customers.

9
00:00:23,244 --> 00:00:30,707
An agent marketplace needs services that already have traffic, and traffic is the
one thing a repo never ships.

10
00:00:31,087 --> 00:00:34,318
Outlive sells the business, not the build.

11
00:00:34,348 --> 00:00:39,094
Every token is an NFT that owns one running paid API.

12
00:00:39,124 --> 00:00:45,881
Inside the token: a vault that holds the money, the price list, the customer ledger,
and the worker key.

13
00:00:45,911 --> 00:00:48,985
Hold the token, and the revenue is yours.

14
00:00:49,415 --> 00:00:52,254
This is the live board on NEAR testnet.

15
00:00:52,284 --> 00:00:57,605
Nine tokens, a few hundred paid calls, every figure read from the contract.

16
00:00:57,635 --> 00:01:00,944
Open one and the whole business is legible.

17
00:01:00,974 --> 00:01:07,235
Owner, worker key, vault, gas spent, and what each holder earned while it was
theirs.

18
00:01:07,615 --> 00:01:10,193
The sale is one transaction.

19
00:01:10,223 --> 00:01:15,543
The token moves, the vault moves with it, and the buyer rotates the worker key.

20
00:01:15,573 --> 00:01:19,118
The old key stops working the moment the sale lands.

21
00:01:19,148 --> 00:01:22,692
Customers keep the same endpoint and the same price.

22
00:01:22,722 --> 00:01:26,919
Forty of forty obligations handed over. None dropped.

23
00:01:27,349 --> 00:01:29,613
We attacked our own protocol.

24
00:01:29,643 --> 00:01:33,031
The old worker key cannot call another method.

25
00:01:33,061 --> 00:01:35,639
No key can withdraw from the vault.

26
00:01:35,669 --> 00:01:41,930
A hostile seller cannot take the buyer's money. The contract refuses before
execution.

27
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:48,299
And when we paid our own customers to look like demand, the appraisal flagged every
one as owner-funded.

28
00:01:48,729 --> 00:01:50,367
The run we recorded.

29
00:01:50,397 --> 00:01:59,871
Sixty-six paid calls in a day. Zero point six six tUSDC of revenue, zero point five
four net after gas.

30
00:01:59,901 --> 00:02:02,975
Four point four days to earn back the price.

31
00:02:03,005 --> 00:02:07,672
The strict policy still rejects it. Too young, too small.

32
00:02:07,702 --> 00:02:11,403
That is the point. The numbers are the numbers.

33
00:02:11,983 --> 00:02:13,124
Outlive.

34
00:02:13,154 --> 00:02:16,228
A business that outlives the person who started it.
